%% ============================================================================
%% Diagram 4 - CI/CD pipeline (manifest-driven)
%% Purpose: how a commit becomes a deployed, verified application.
%% Every stage reads stack.json (the single source of truth for the stack),
%% so both engines (GitHub Actions / Jenkins) share the same scripts and a new
%% service needs only a stack.json entry.
%% ============================================================================
flowchart TD
    DEV[Developer] -->|git push to main| GH[GitHub / Jenkins]
    GH -->|triggers Deploy pipeline| CH[Checkout]
    CH --> VAL[stack-validate<br/>validate stack.json manifest]
    VAL --> CI[CI per service - stack-ci.sh<br/>ci_steps in toolchain + Docker build + Trivy scan]
    CI -->|pass| LOGIN[ECR login]
    LOGIN --> PUSH[stack-push<br/>build + push every service :git-sha]
    PUSH --> DEPLOY[deploy-ec2<br/>update SSM image params per service<br/>+ start ASG instance refresh]
    PUSH --> DEPK[optional: deploy-eks<br/>render k8s manifests from stack.json + apply]
    DEPLOY --> SMOKE[Smoke test against ALB]
    DEPK --> SMOKE2[Smoke test against NLB]
    SMOKE -->|healthy| DONE[Deployed to EC2 ✓]
    SMOKE2 -->|healthy| DONE2[Deployed to EKS ✓]

    CI -->|scan finds issues| BLOCK[Pipeline fails - nothing deployed]

    PR[PR / push to develop] --> CICFG
    subgraph CICFG[CI workflow - ci.yml / Jenkinsfile-ci]
        A[stack-validate] --> B[stack-ci: test + audit + build + Trivy] --> C[Terraform fmt + validate]
    end